/**
 * The `overflow-x` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property sets what shows
 * when content overflows a block-level element's left and right edges. This may be nothing, a
 * scroll bar, or the overflow content. This property may also be set by using the `overflow`
 * shorthand property.
 *
 * Initial: visible. Inherited: no.
 * Percentages: not accepted.
 *
 * Grammar: visible | hidden | clip | scroll | auto
 *
 * Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-overflow-3/#propdef-overflow-x
